.TH "GLESHA-IMPORT" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-import \- add an existing full archive to a set
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha import\fR SET \-\-file FILE [options]
.br
\fBglesha import\fR SET \-\-file FILE \-\-from REMOTE [\-\-key KEY] [options]
.br
\fBglesha import\fR SET \-\-from REMOTE \-\-key KEY [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an existing full archive as a snapshot of SET. SET is created if it does not exist.
.PP
With \-\-file only, the local archive is imported. With \-\-file and \-\-from, the archive is also associated with its uploaded copy at KEY, which is checked by size, or by content with \-\-deep\-verify; nothing is uploaded. With \-\-from and \-\-key only, the object is downloaded and imported.
.PP
Imported roots are not bound to local directories. Use \-\-root, or 'glesha configure SET \-\-root', before running backups.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-file FILE
Local archive to import.
.TP
.B \-\-key KEY
Object key (default with \-\-file: the file name).
.TP
.B \-\-root NAME=PATH
Bind root NAME to directory PATH; repeatable. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-baseline new
Use as the next incremental's baseline.
.TP
.B \-\-date DATE
Original backup time, in RFC 3339 format. For example, 2024\-05\-01T12:00:00Z.
.TP
.B \-\-deep\-verify
Compare content with the uploaded copy, not size.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Remotes holding the archive, tried in order.
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the archive passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). A trailing newline is ignored. Without this option, the passphrase is read from a hidden prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.SS Retrieval options
.TP
.B \-\-request\-retrieval
Allow charged cold retrieval without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-retrieval TIER
Tier: bulk, standard, or expedited (default: bulk). The default comes from the [cold] tier setting.
.TP
.B \-\-days N
Keep retrieved copies for N days (default: 3). The default comes from the [cold] days setting. A pending request keeps its original duration.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. If available memory cannot be determined, 128MiB is used.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha import old\-docs \-\-file old\-backup.tar.gz.gpg
glesha import old\-docs \-\-from b2 \-\-key backups/old\-backup.tar.gz.gpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-archive (1),
.BR glesha\-configure (1)
